// Every material's lexicon: the words its letters may form up close.
//
// name      what its letters spell now and then: an easter egg, met at the first or second look
// elements  what it is made of, spelled more often than its name; at most three
// hot       what its letters say as it heats, from least to most; at most three
// cold      and as it cools; at most two
//
// One entry for every material of the full game, keyed as in `materials.ron`. A material is
// baked with the lexicon of its key. The table in full-game/docs/brief/2-art-direction.md is
// this file written out; a test fails if the two disagree. Every word is printable ASCII.
// The Erasure has no words: it is being erased.
[
    (key: "masonry", name: "stone", elements: ["SiO2", "CaCO3", "Al2O3"], hot: ["HOT", "CRACKING", "GLOWING"], cold: ["COLD", "FROSTED"]),
